---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Rivett · I find where revenue leaks. Then I fix the system."
  description="A senior growth practice for profitable US operators. Request the gated audit, diagnose the leaks, and rebuild the system between demand and revenue."
  fontWeights="Inter+Tight:wght@400;500;600;700;800"
  currentNav="home"
>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/audit/v3-css/kit.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/audit/v3-css/audit.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/audit/v3-css/v2.css" />

  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
    <symbol id="ic-diagnostic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="6"/><path d="M15.5 15.5 L20 20"/><circle class="dot" cx="11" cy="11" r="1.4" fill="var(--accent)" stroke="none"/></symbol>
    <symbol id="ic-stack" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M3 7 L12 3 L21 7 L12 11 Z"/><path d="M3 12 L12 16 L21 12"/><path d="M3 17 L12 21 L21 17"/></symbol>
    <symbol id="ic-cadence" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 6 V12 L17 14"/></symbol>
  </svg>

  <!-- Thin accent line at top of viewport showing scroll progress. Pure
       presentational; hidden when prefers-reduced-motion. -->
  <div class="scroll-progress" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="scroll-progress-fill" id="scrollProgressFill"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="page audit-first-home">

    <!-- Hero (audit-first) -->
    <header class="audit-hero">
      <span class="stamp">Ran growth at Somewhere.com · $100M+ managed</span>
      <h1><span class="sheen">I find where revenue leaks.</span> <br/><span class="ital">Then I fix the system.</span></h1>
      <p class="dek">I work with profitable US operators to find the expensive leaks between demand and revenue, then rebuild the reporting, handoffs, follow-up, and AI-assisted workflows that keep money moving.</p>

      <form class="audit-form" method="POST" action="/audit/v3" id="homeAuditForm">
        <span class="prefix">https://</span>
        <input class="domain" type="text" name="url" inputmode="url" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="none" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="enter the site you want read" required aria-label="Domain" />
        <input type="hidden" name="source" value="home" />
        <button class="btn btn--solid btn--with-dot" type="submit" data-cta="home_audit_form_submit">
          <span class="btn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          Run audit <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </button>
      </form>

      <div class="audit-meta">
        <span><b>~30s</b> to run</span>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span><b>9</b> dimensions</span>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>ranked fix list</span>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>operator field note</span>
      </div>

      {/* Past-employer marquee · CF-style horizontal scroll of credibility
          wordmarks. Doubles the content so the loop is seamless. */}
      <div class="hero-marquee" aria-label="Past employers" role="region">
        <div class="hero-marquee-track">
          <span class="hm-item">Somewhere</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">Unilever</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">Samsung</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">Visa</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">Vodafone</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">$100M+ managed</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">4 continents</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item">15 years</span>
          <span class="hm-sep">·</span>
          {/* Duplicate set so the scroll loops without a visible jump */}
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">Somewhere</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">Unilever</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">Samsung</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">Visa</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">Vodafone</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">$100M+ managed</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">4 continents</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="hm-item" aria-hidden="true">15 years</span>
          <span class="hm-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- 01 · The work -->
    <div class="sec-head" id="work">
      <span class="lbl">The work<span class="num">01</span></span>
      <h2>A fixed path <span class="ital">from leak to operating rhythm.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p class="lede">First I find the leaks. Then I build the highest-value fixes. If the rhythm matters enough to keep, I run the system with dashboards, alerts, weekly decisions, and board-grade summaries.</p>

      <div class="modules">
        <div class="mod">
          <div class="head">
            <svg class="ic" width="24" height="24"><use href="#ic-diagnostic"/></svg>
            <span class="mod-code">M · 01</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Diagnostic. <span class="ital">Two weeks.</span></h3>
          <p>Find the leaks, name the constraints, and decide what is worth fixing. Acquisition + channel teardown, funnel + lifecycle audit, tooling + AI workflow review, prioritised 90-day fix list.</p>
          <div class="meta">
            <span><b>02</b> wks</span>
            <span>One memo <span class="ital">fixed scope</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mod">
          <div class="head">
            <svg class="ic" width="24" height="24"><use href="#ic-stack"/></svg>
            <span class="mod-code">M · 02</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Build. <span class="ital">Stack + instrumentation.</span></h3>
          <p>Rebuild acquisition and revenue operations around the highest-value fixes. Paid media, SEO foundations, lifecycle + CRM, AI-assisted workflows with approval gates.</p>
          <div class="meta">
            <span><b>04–06</b> wks</span>
            <span>Scoped <span class="ital">after M01</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mod">
          <div class="head">
            <svg class="ic" width="24" height="24"><use href="#ic-cadence"/></svg>
            <span class="mod-code">M · 03</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Run. <span class="ital">Cadence over volume.</span></h3>
          <p>Maintain the weekly rhythm that keeps revenue moving. Working sessions, live dashboard + alerting, monthly board summary. Cancel any month.</p>
          <div class="meta">
            <span><b>Monthly</b></span>
            <span>Scoped <span class="ital">after M01</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="post-note">M01 fee credits in full toward M02 if you continue. <span class="ital">No long contracts. No retainer creep.</span></p>
    </div>

    <!-- 02 · Who this is for -->
    <div class="sec-head" id="who">
      <span class="lbl">Who this is for<span class="num">02</span></span>
      <h2>Operators of profitable, <span class="ital">un-glamorous businesses.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p class="lede">Real revenue, ready to compound. You already have demand. The problem is what happens around it.</p>

      <div class="audience">
        <div class="col">
          <span class="stamp">01 · Real estate</span>
          <h4>Operators <span class="ital">+ brokerages.</span></h4>
          <p>Self-storage, multifamily, brokerage, REPE. Capital raise, sphere and farm, leasing pipeline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <span class="stamp">02 · Services</span>
          <h4>Boring, profitable, <span class="ital">growing.</span></h4>
          <p>Construction, manufacturing, professional services, agency owners. 50–500 people, real revenue, ready to compound.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <span class="stamp">03 · Mid-market</span>
          <h4>Founders <span class="ital">+ operators.</span></h4>
          <p>50–500 people, profitable, ready to compound. You do not want a slick agency. You want senior judgment on the growth system underneath the business.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="exclusion">
        <span class="stamp stamp--neutral">If you do not see yourself here</span>
        <p>Email me anyway. I will tell you straight if I am the wrong call. <span class="ital">Probably not: you want a junior to take orders, a yes-person, or a generic AI roadmap.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 03 · Track record -->
    <div class="sec-head" id="about">
      <span class="lbl">Track record<span class="num">03</span></span>
      <h2>Fifteen years inside acquisition. <span class="ital">Now applied to the whole system.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <div class="bio">
        <div class="bio-l">
          <span class="stamp stamp--neutral">Founder · operator · sole point of contact</span>
          <h3 class="bio-name">Fred Style.</h3>
          <p class="bio-tag"><span class="ital">Paid acquisition is the proof. Revenue operations are the work.</span></p>
          <p class="bio-body">Fifteen years on growth at <b>Somewhere</b>, <b>Unilever</b>, <b>Samsung</b>, <b>Visa</b>, and <b>Vodafone</b>. <span class="ital">In-house, agency, and vendor.</span> Most recently a year running growth at Somewhere.com, the global recruiting platform. Roughly $100M in managed spend across four continents.</p>
          <p class="bio-body">Independent. Cape Town based. Available to a small number of operators per quarter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bio-r">
          <figure class="bio-portrait">
            <div class="pre">
              <span>Portrait · <b>Fred Style</b> · Cape Town</span>
              <span>2026·05</span>
            </div>
            <div class="frame">
              <img src="/img/fred.png" alt="Portrait of Fred Style" width="800" height="800" />
            </div>
            <div class="post">
              <span class="name">Fred Style.</span>
              <span class="role">Founder · operator · <span class="ital">sole point of contact</span></span>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: var(--sp-10);">
        <div class="numbox">
          <div><span class="k">Career</span><span class="v">15 <span class="ital">yrs</span></span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Managed spend</span><span class="v">$100M <span class="ital">+</span></span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Continents</span><span class="v">04 <span class="ital"></span></span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Sectors</span><span class="v">05 <span class="ital">+</span></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proof">
        <span class="stamp">Proof from the work</span>
        <h4 class="proof-h">Before selling the system, <span class="ital">I ran it on my own pipeline for 90 days.</span></h4>
        <p class="proof-body">The first hard failure was caught internally, rebuilt, and turned into the approval discipline clients get.</p>
        <div class="numbox">
          <div><span class="k">Throughput</span><span class="v">10 <span class="ital">/ hr to queue</span></span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Review rhythm</span><span class="v">80 <span class="ital">/ day at pace</span></span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Calibration</span><span class="v">60–85 <span class="ital">% by week 12</span></span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Failure caught</span><span class="v">0 / 15 <span class="ital">ICP miss</span></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 04 · The deal -->
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="lbl">The deal<span class="num">04</span></span>
      <h2>Senior judgment. <span class="ital">Different cost structure. No agency markup.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p class="lede">I work from Cape Town by design. The advantage is not "cheap." It is structural: direct access to the operator doing the work, senior growth judgment on the system, and AI-assisted execution underneath without paying for a US agency org chart.</p>

      <table class="deal-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Senior growth support</th>
            <th class="r">Annualised</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>US agency, retainer</td>
            <td class="r">$300–500k</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>In-house VP marketing</td>
            <td class="r">$220–280k</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Boutique consultancy</td>
            <td class="r">$180–240k</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hi">
            <td><b>Rivett · M03 retainer</b></td>
            <td class="r"><b>~⅓ <span class="ital">of the above</span></b></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- 05 · AI in the work -->
    <div class="sec-head" id="approach">
      <span class="lbl">AI in the work<span class="num">05</span></span>
      <h2>AI belongs <span class="ital">below the judgment layer.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p class="lede">The valuable work is deciding what matters. AI belongs underneath that judgment, not in place of it. Most agencies are now selling the busywork as the product. I am selling senior judgment, with the busywork automated underneath. <span class="ital">Different deal.</span></p>

      <div class="two-col">
        <div class="col">
          <span class="stamp">What I automate</span>
          <ul class="bare">
            <li>Lead enrichment + routing.</li>
            <li>Draft outreach + sequencing.</li>
            <li>Daily, weekly reporting.</li>
            <li>Anomaly + spend alerts.</li>
            <li>Content briefs at scale.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col col-r">
          <span class="stamp stamp--neutral">What stays human</span>
          <ul class="bare">
            <li>Audience + positioning calls.</li>
            <li>Channel mix + budget.</li>
            <li>Creative + message strategy.</li>
            <li>Pricing + offer design.</li>
            <li><span class="ital">The hard conversation about why it is not working.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Pull quote -->
    <div class="pull">
      <blockquote>"Run the audit. If it finds a real leak, book a call and I will walk you through the full read. The diagnostic turns that signal into a one-page memo with the halt list and the next 90 days. Two weeks, fixed scope."</blockquote>
      <cite>— Section 06 · next step</cite>
    </div>

    <!-- End CTA · dark closer -->
    <div class="end-cta" id="contact">
      <h3>Ready to find the leaks? <span class="ital">Run the audit.</span></h3>
      <div class="right">
        <span class="stamp stamp--on-ink">9 dimensions · ranked fixes · operator field note</span>
        <p>Enter your site, see where the revenue leaks. If the read points at something real, book a call and I will walk you through the full diagnostic.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--inv" data-cta="home_closer_run_audit" href="#homeAuditForm">Run audit <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Live scan overlay · animates while /audit/v3 POST is in flight.
         Markup + CSS + JS lifted from src/pages/audit/v3.astro (commit 32518b6).
         Browser POSTs the form to /audit/v3; this overlay covers the homepage
         and animates until the response swaps the page. -->
    <div class="scan on-ink" id="scanOverlay" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="scan-top">
        <span><span class="dot-live"></span>Live scan · <b id="scanDomain">somewhere.com</b></span>
        <a class="wordmark">rivett<span class="dot-mark" style="background: var(--accent);"></span></a>
        <span><b>v3.4</b> · in-browser only</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scan-body">
        <div class="scan-log">
          <div class="log-head">stdout · run · audit.v3</div>
          <div class="log-list" id="logList"></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="scan-side">
          <h3>Reading the curve. <span class="ital">No deck. Just the numbers.</span></h3>
          <div class="progress">
            <div>
              <span class="label">Scan progress</span>
              <div class="pct"><span id="pctVal">0</span><sup>/100</sup></div>
            </div>
            <span class="label" id="elapsed">00.0s</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bar"><div class="fill" id="barFill"></div></div>
          <div style="margin-top: var(--sp-7);">
            <div class="lane" data-lane="0"><span class="ix">D · 01</span><span class="nm">Google index</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="1"><span class="ix">D · 02</span><span class="nm">AI engines</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="2"><span class="ix">D · 03</span><span class="nm">Page speed</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="3"><span class="ix">D · 04</span><span class="nm">Measurement</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="4"><span class="ix">D · 05</span><span class="nm">Ad libraries</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="5"><span class="ix">D · 06</span><span class="nm">Conversion</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="6"><span class="ix">D · 07</span><span class="nm">Mobile render</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="7"><span class="ix">D · 08</span><span class="nm">Email auth (DoH)</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
            <div class="lane" data-lane="8"><span class="ix">D · 09</span><span class="nm">Tech fingerprint</span><span class="st">queued</span></div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Site footer (mock SiteFooter pattern) -->
  <footer class="site-foot">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="row">
        <div>
          <a href="/" class="wm wm--inv" aria-label="Rivett, home">
            rivett<span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <span class="col-h">The work</span>
          <a href="#work">Diagnostic</a>
          <a href="#work">Build</a>
          <a href="#work">Run</a>
          <a href="#homeAuditForm" data-cta="home_footer_run_audit">Run audit</a>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <span class="col-h">Field notes</span>
          <a href="/blog">All notes</a>
          <a href="/blog">Cadence</a>
          <a href="/blog">Instrumentation</a>
          <a href="/blog">Decline</a>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <span class="col-h">Contact</span>
          <a href="mailto:fred@rivett.tech">fred@rivett.tech</a>
          <a href="/diagnostic">Talk to Fred</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/fredstyle/">LinkedIn</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bot">
        <span>© rivett · 2026</span>
        <span>v1.0 · Cape Town &amp; remote</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* v2.css is the source of truth for .audit-hero, .sec-head, .sec-body,
     .modules, .mod, .audience, .lede, .post-note, .exclusion, .bio,
     .bio-portrait, .bio-name, .bio-tag, .bio-body, .proof, .deal-table,
     .two-col, .pull, .end-cta, .numbox. Don't override here - just
     position the page chrome and account for the site Nav above. */
  body { background: var(--paper, #f6f4ef); }
  body main { display: block; }
  .audit-first-home {
    max-width: var(--page-max, 1240px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--page-pad, 32px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .audit-first-home { padding: 0 24px; }
  }
  /* Tighten the audit-hero top padding since our site Nav already sits above
     the page (the mock's .page has its own Nav inside). */
  .audit-first-home .audit-hero { padding-top: var(--sp-10, 48px); }

  .audit-first-home .audit-sample {
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .audit-first-home .audit-sample .sample-note {
    max-width: 780px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* -------- hero motion (CF-inspired, restrained for operator brand) -------- */

  /* Slow oblique sheen across the H1 main line ("I find where revenue
     leaks."). Reads as ambient ink with a green accent sweep, not as a
     loud animation. 9s ease-in-out fits the larger type. */
  .audit-first-home .audit-hero h1 .sheen {
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--ink, #0E1A2C) 0%,
      var(--ink, #0E1A2C) 38%,
      rgba(143, 191, 63, 0.65) 50%,
      var(--ink, #0E1A2C) 62%,
      var(--ink, #0E1A2C) 100%
    );
    background-size: 240% 100%;
    background-position: 100% 0;
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    color: transparent;
    animation: hero-h1-sheen 9s ease-in-out infinite;
    animation-delay: 1.5s;
  }
  @keyframes hero-h1-sheen {
    0%, 100% { background-position: 100% 0; }
    50% { background-position: -20% 0; }
  }

  /* Pulsing accent dot inside the form submit button. Same pattern as
     .dot-live on /audit/v3, just sized for an inline button context. */
  .audit-first-home .audit-form .btn--with-dot {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .audit-first-home .audit-form .btn-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent, #8FBF3F);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(143, 191, 63, 0.6);
    animation: home-btn-dot-pulse 2.2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes home-btn-dot-pulse {
    0%, 100% {
      transform: scale(1);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(143, 191, 63, 0.55);
    }
    50% {
      transform: scale(1.15);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px rgba(143, 191, 63, 0);
    }
  }

  /* Horizontal credibility marquee under the audit-meta row.
     Mask-image fades the edges. Pauses on hover (CF pattern). */
  .audit-first-home .hero-marquee {
    margin-top: var(--sp-7, 36px);
    overflow: hidden;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 760px;
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0,
      black 8%,
      black 92%,
      transparent 100%
    );
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0,
      black 8%,
      black 92%,
      transparent 100%
    );
  }
  .audit-first-home .hero-marquee-track {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    animation: hero-marquee-scroll 38s linear infinite;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .audit-first-home .hero-marquee:hover .hero-marquee-track {
    animation-play-state: paused;
  }
  .audit-first-home .hm-item {
    font-family: var(--mono, 'DM Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-dim, #4a5468);
    padding: 0 14px;
  }
  .audit-first-home .hm-sep {
    color: var(--accent, #8FBF3F);
